            <ArticleTitle>Inhibition of tissue prostaglandin synthesis during third molar surgery: use of preoperative fenbufen.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>251-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Preoperative administration of a non-steroidal anti-inflammatory drug (fenbufen) reduced immediate postoperative pain in a group of 38 patients undergoing removal of mandibular third molars, compared to placebo. However, overall pain experience and morbidity were not significantly improved suggesting that there was no clinical benefit derived from interference with tissue prostaglandin synthesis at the time of surgery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
